{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>As he approached.</b> His camp, or it is among the intransitive verbs, for there are found verbs that are both transitive and intransitive." "And the word נא is like 'now,' and likewise \"הנה נא זקנתי\" (Genesis 27:2), \"אוי נא לנו\" (Lamentations 5:16), and it is reversed in the Ishmaelite language." "And the sense of \"הנה נא ידעתי\" is that Sarah's beauty was known only in her own land and in Egypt, but the land of the Negev was not like it, for complexions change on account of the air." "And the sense of ואותך יהי׳ is that they would give you all your needs, for they were days of famine:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:21.843022321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}